CM 20-Meter Bobtail Curtain Antenna Model
CM Designed for ~14.2 MHz over Saltwater / Beach
CM Bidirectional broadside pattern with vertical polarization.
CM  --- Symbols / Variables ---
CM  --- Calculations derived from elements ---
CM  --- Geometry Cards (GW: Tag, Segments, X1, Y1, Z1, X2, Y2, Z2, Radius) ---
CM  1. Left Vertical Element
CM  2. Left Horizontal Phasing Section
CM  3. Right Horizontal Phasing Section
CM  4. Right Vertical Element
CM  5. Center Vertical Element (Split into 2 wires to force an exact center feed segment)
CM  --- End of Geometry ---
CM  --- Ground Control (Real Ground / Average Soil) ---
CM  --- Source / Excitation (Voltage feed at the center of the middle vertical) ---
CM  Fed at wire 5, segment 7 (top segment of the lower half, creating a center feed)
CM  --- Frequency Setup ---
CM  --- Execution Commands ---
CE
SY freq=14.2	'Design Frequency in MHz
SY rad=.00506	'Wire radius (#12 AWG copper wire)
SY h_top=20	'Height of horizontal top wire above ground (feet)
SY l_vert=16.04	'Length of the 1/4-wavelength vertical elements (feet)
SY l_space=32.08	'Spacing between verticals (~1/2-wavelength phasing, feet)
SY h_bot=h_top-l_vert	'Clearance of the bottom tips from the ground
GW	1	15	0	-l_space	h_bot	0	-l_space	h_top	rad	'1/4 side
GW	2	25	0	-l_space	h_top	0	0	h_top	rad	'1/2 wave top
GW	3	25	0	0	h_top	0	l_space	h_top	rad	'1/2 wave top
GW	4	15	0	l_space	h_bot	0	l_space	h_top	rad	'1/4 wave side
GW	5	7	0	0	h_bot	0	0	(h_bot+l_vert/2)	rad	'1/8 wave feedpoint
GW	6	7	0	0	(h_bot+l_vert/2)	0	0	h_top	rad	'1/8 wave
GE	-1
GN	3	0	0	0	81	5.0
EK
EX	0	5	7	0	1	0	0	'Seg 5 & 6 are a 1/4 1:1 dipole loaded
FR	0	0	0	0	freq	0
EN
